{
  "format": "lcir.lesson",
  "formatVersion": 3,
  "id": "adders",
  "title": "Adders: sum and carry",
  "workbench": "circuit",
  "board": "full-adder",
  "steps": [
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "A **half adder** adds two bits. The **sum** is A XOR B and the **carry** is A AND B. The full adder here is two half adders and an OR gate.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "power", "on": true },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["ha1"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "1 + 0 + 0. One input is high, so **SUM** = 1 and **COUT** = 0. There is nothing to carry.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 1, "set": [1, 0, 0], "when": "open" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["a", "b", "cin", "lsum", "lcout"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Now 1 + 1 + 0. What do **SUM** and **COUT** show?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "SUM = 1, COUT = 0" },
        { "text": "SUM = 0, COUT = 1", "right": true },
        { "text": "SUM = 1, COUT = 1" },
        { "text": "SUM = 0, COUT = 0" }
      ],
      "answer": "1 + 1 = 10 in binary. The low bit is 0 (XOR of two equal inputs) and the 1 is the carry (AND of two ones).",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 2, "set": [1, 1, 0], "when": "reveal" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["ha1", "lsum", "lcout"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Now 1 + 1 + 1, with a carry coming in. What do **SUM** and **COUT** show?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "SUM = 0, COUT = 1" },
        { "text": "SUM = 1, COUT = 1", "right": true },
        { "text": "SUM = 1, COUT = 0" }
      ],
      "answer": "1 + 1 + 1 = 11 in binary, so both bits are 1. SUM is the XOR of all three inputs, and COUT is 1 when at least two inputs are 1.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 3, "set": [1, 1, 1], "when": "reveal" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["lsum", "lcout"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "How it got there: the first half adder turns 1 + 1 into sum 0, carry 1. The second adds **CIN** to that sum, giving sum 1, carry 0. The OR gate merges the two carries.",
      "actions": [{ "kind": "highlight", "components": ["ha1", "ha2", "orc"] }]
    },
    {
      "kind": "predict",
      "prose": "Last case, 0 + 1 + 1. Which outputs are 1?",
      "choices": [
        { "text": "SUM only" },
        { "text": "COUT only", "right": true },
        { "text": "Both" },
        { "text": "Neither" }
      ],
      "answer": "Two ones add to 10: SUM = 0 and COUT = 1. The carry out is the majority of A, B and CIN, whichever two of them are high.",
      "actions": [
        { "kind": "row", "index": 4, "set": [0, 1, 1], "when": "reveal" },
        { "kind": "highlight", "components": ["lsum", "lcout"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "narrate",
      "prose": "Remember the two rules: **SUM** = A XOR B XOR CIN (an odd number of ones), **COUT** = majority of A, B, CIN. Play the rest of the sequence with `]` and predict each row first.",
      "actions": [{ "kind": "tab", "tab": "sequence" }]
    }
  ]
}
